Reason: Lazy room loading freed a persistent room's tile array on leave while its saved layers still pointed into it; back from AM2R's pause screen the ground was drawn from the pause room's tileset.
Upstream: Engine bug (lazyLoadRooms + persistent rooms) on every platform - to offer upstream as a fork branch. Retires this patch when merged.

--- a/src/runner.c
+++ b/src/runner.c
@@ -3780,7 +3780,8 @@
         }
 
         // Free the outgoing room's payload under lazyLoadRooms, unless it's eagerly pinned or we're restarting the same room (initRoom would just re-load it).
-        if (runner->dataWin->lazyLoadRooms && !oldRoom->eagerlyLoaded && newRoomIndex != oldRoomIndex) {
+        // A persistent room's saved layers borrow its tile array, so that payload stays until the room is left for good.
+        if (runner->dataWin->lazyLoadRooms && !oldRoom->eagerlyLoaded && newRoomIndex != oldRoomIndex && !oldRoom->persistent) {
             DataWin_freeRoomPayload(oldRoom);
         }
 
